## What the official site says

Rockstar’s Grand Theft Auto VI page lists November 19, 2026 for PlayStation 5 and Xbox Series X|S. That date was checked on October 16, 2026. Treat it as the publisher’s stated target, not a promise that the date cannot move. The place to confirm any change is [Rockstar’s GTA VI page](https://www.rockstargames.com/VI).

This is a separate game from Grand Theft Auto V Enhanced, which is already released on PC. The Enhanced edition has its own [Steam listing](/apps/gta-v-enhanced).

## Official updates already posted

On October 15, 2026, Rockstar featured the GTA VI launch trailer on its newswire. Watch that video on [Rockstar’s trailer post](https://www.rockstargames.com/newswire/article/517572321a549a), not a re-upload.

On October 8, 2026, Rockstar posted about the in-game radio stations and the music of Leonida. The lineup and details are in [that announcement](https://www.rockstargames.com/newswire/article/o3982oa93a23k4/the-music-of-grand-theft-auto-vi-in-game-radio-stations).

## What this page does not claim

This is a dated editorial snapshot. It is not a hands-on preview, a PC release date, or a list of system requirements. GameNews is not affiliated with Rockstar. When a newer official post appears, use the publisher’s page rather than an older recap.
